    "visibleText": "ROS2Lab ROS 2 for beginners\nHome\nPlayground\nSimulator\nFree resources\nLog in\nRegister\nRobotic Models Simulator / TurtleBot3 Waffle\nTurtleBot3 Waffle\n\nThis page has the maker's own ROS 2 Jazzy workspace for TurtleBot3 Waffle, cloned from GitHub at pinned commits. Build it with colcon, source it, and start it with the same ros2 launch commands as on Ubuntu: the real launch files run, and Gazebo, RViz2, ros2_control, Nav2 and MoveIt 2 are ROS2Lab's models of those programs.\n\nMobile robots · ROBOTIS\n\nTurtleBot3 Waffle\n\nDifferential-drive research robot with an LDS-01 360° lidar, an RGB camera and an IMU.\n\nOfficial ROS 2 Jazzy workspace\n\nTurtleBot3 (ROBOTIS) - ROS 2 Jazzy. 7 repositories at pinned commits, 18 packages, in ~/ros2_ws/src.\n\nROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3 @ 0c0be84e (jazzy, Apache-2.0)\nROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_msgs @ 9209e01b (jazzy, Apache-2.0)\nROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_simulations @ 45633014 (jazzy, Apache-2.0)\nROBOTIS-GIT/DynamixelSDK @ 516ae863 (jazzy, Apache-2.0)\nROBOTIS-GIT/hls_lfcd_lds_driver @ 6a80b3f1 (jazzy, BSD-3-Clause)\nROBOTIS-GIT/ld08_driver @ 00dba810 (jazzy, Apache-2.0)\nROBOTIS-GIT/coin_d4_driver @ 79d18332 (jazzy, Apache-2.0)\nSIMULATION\nGazebo: TurtleBot3 World\nros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py\nGazebo: empty world\nros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo empty_world.launch.py\nGazebo: TurtleBot3 House\nros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_house.launch.py\nSLAM with Cartographer (run with a Gazebo world)\nros2 launch turtlebot3_cartographer cartographer.launch.py use_sim_time:=True\nSave the map\nros2 run nav2_map_server map_saver_cli -f ~/map\nNav2 with the map shipped in turtlebot3_navigation2 (TurtleBot3 World)\nros2 launch turtlebot3_navigation2 navigation2.launch.py use_sim_time:=True\nNavigation2 with a saved map (run with a Gazebo world)\nros2 launch turtlebot3_navigation2 navigation2.launch.py use_sim_time:=True map:=$HOME/map.yaml\nKeyboard teleoperation\nros2 run turtlebot3_teleop teleop_keyboard\nRobot model in RViz\nros2 launch turtlebot3_bringup rviz2.launch.py\nFake node (no physics) + RViz\nros2 launch turtlebot3_fake_node turtlebot3_fake_node.launch.py\nREAL HARDWARE\nReal TurtleBot3 (run on the robot's Raspberry Pi)\nros2 launch turtlebot3_bringup robot.launch.py\n\nStarts the maker's driver for the real robot. It needs a hardware license from your course administrator, and the robot connected to the computer that runs ROS 2 (use \"Connect to ROS 2 on your Ubuntu computer\" below to see it here).\n\nThe same workspace on your Ubuntu 24.04 computer\n\nThe launch files, URDF/xacro, SDF worlds, YAML and RViz configs are the makers' own files, run by the real ROS 2 launch library in your browser. Gazebo, Nav2, MoveIt 2 and the drivers are ROS2Lab's models of those programs, not the compiled programs themselves.\n\nWorkspace files (18 packages; open them in VS Code with: code ~/ros2_ws)\nRobot details: links, joints, sensors, Gazebo plugins\nTerminal: ~/ros2_ws\nstudent@ros2lab: ~/ros2_ws\nRight-click a terminal for the Terminator menu\n+ New terminal\nstudent@ros2lab: ~/ros2_ws\nrviz2\nstudent@ros2lab:~/ros2_ws$ TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=waffle ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py\nPackage 'turtlebot3_gazebo' not found: \"package 'turtlebot3_gazebo' not found, searching: ['/opt/ros/jazzy']\"\nInstall it with apt (the apt name uses dashes: ros-jazzy-...), then source again.\n(Loading the official ROS 2 Jazzy workspace of TurtleBot3 Waffle…)\n(TurtleBot3 Waffle: the makers' packages are in ~/ros2_ws/src. Build with colcon build, source install/setup.bash, export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=waffle, then launch. Pick a command above, or type it.)\nstudent@ros2lab:~/ros2_ws$ ros2 run rviz2 rviz2\n[INFO] [rviz2]: Stereo is NOT SUPPORTED\n[INFO] [rviz2]: OpenGl version: 4.6 (GLSL 4.6)\n(The RViz2 window opened below the terminal.)\n/rviz2 is running in this terminal. Real ROS 2 works the same way: open a + New terminal to type more commands.\nCtrl+C (stop it)\nTab\n↑ Last command\nOpen a new terminal\nOpen VS Code\nStart again\nRViz\nFile\nPanels\nHelp\nInteract\nMove Camera\nSelect\nFocus Camera\nMeasure\n2D Pose Estimate\n2D Goal Pose\nPublish Point\nDisplays\nGlobal Options\nFixed Frame\nBackground Color\n48; 48; 48\nFrame Rate\n30\nGlobal Status: Error\nFixed Frame\nFixed Frame [map] does not exist\nGrid\nAdd\nDuplicate\nRemove\nRename\n3D Orbit\n2D Top\nViews\nType:\nOrbit (rviz_default_plugins)\nFPS (rviz_default_plugins)\nThirdPersonFollower (rviz_default_plugins)\nTopDownOrtho (rviz_default_plugins)\nXYOrbit (rviz_default_plugins)\nZero\nCurrent View\nOrbit (rviz_default_plugins)\nNear Clip Distance\n0.01\nInvert Z Axis\nTarget Frame\n<Fixed Frame>\nDistance\n10\nFocal Shape Size\n0.05\nFocal Shape Fixed Size\nYaw\n0.785398\nPitch\n0.785398\nFocal Point\n0; 0; 0\nSave\nRemove\nRename\nTime\nROS Time:\nROS Elapsed:\nWall Time:\nWall Elapsed:\nExperimental\nReset\nLeft-Click: Rotate. Middle-Click: Move X/Y. Right-Click/Mouse Wheel: Zoom. Shift: More options.\nFixed Frame: Fixed Frame [map] does not exist\nGrid: Fixed Frame [map] does not exist\nConnect to ROS 2 on your Ubuntu computer (rosbridge)\nHow it works, and its limits\nROS2Lab: a free ROS 2 course for students and engineers\nDeveloped by the Robotics and ROS2 lab Channel\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy notice",
